// Real-spawn attempt, banked RED (2026-07-24): the scheduled fanout under
// parallel_compose, the Threaded schedule read live from the install chain.
// Compiles with zero diagnostics; runs to exit 134 — `unaligned atomic` in
// ffi_join <- op_parallel_compose_thread_join <- main — identically through
// mentl-runner and the 43.0.1 CLI. The sequential twin
// (tests/frontier/mn-scheduled-fanout-int.mn ~> sequential_compose) answers
// 60 through both. The trap is guest glue, not host: spawn's return value
// (a thread id under any real wasi-threads host) rides ThreadHandle while
// ffi_join dereferences the payload as a closure pointer. Compile with the
// frontier RTLIBS (memory strings lists threading prelude).
fn widen(x) = x * 15

fn main() = {
  let (a, b) = (2 <| (widen, widen)) ~> parallel_compose ~> wasi_threads
  a + b
}
